      "writtenOn": "2022-03-07T07:31:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I understand your code correct, `base_enable_allow` can be determined from the current power state like:\n\n`bool base_enable_allow \u003d !chipset_in_state(CHIPSET_STATE_ANY_OFF)`\n\nno need to add the global variable.",
      "revId": "75381a0c1e20234ac89b879ead26ff9d62a52e09",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c01c3dc_c6bab49e",
        "filename": "board/mrbland/base_detect.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1512583
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-08T01:48:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Use !chipset_in_state(CHIPSET_STATE_ANY_OFF) as flag will cause the keyboard power \n keeping on when DUT transfor S0 to G3. That is because base_disable() is called in POWER_S3S5 while the chipset state is (CHIPSET_STATE_SOFT_OFF|CHIPSET_STATE_SUSPEND). Then in base_detect_change() the base_enable_allow flag is still true, and the function will return immediately, so the keyboard power still keep on.",
      "parentUuid": "7b8d8730_f008fc3e",
      "revId": "75381a0c1e20234ac89b879ead26ff9d62a52e09",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
